\b MyDesktop\b0\par
\par
MyDesktop arranges the icons already on your desktop into fences. It does not move, copy or delete your files on its own: putting an item into a fence changes where it is drawn, not where it is stored.\par
\par
While MyDesktop is running it switches off the Windows desktop icon layer and draws the desktop itself. It switches that layer back on when it exits. If the program is ended abnormally the icons can be left hidden; right-click the desktop and choose View, then Show desktop icons, to bring them back.\par
